<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jáchymov</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Joachimsthal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jáchymov, in German Joachimsthal, is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ore-mountains">Ore Mountains</a> of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czechia</a>, founded after rich <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> deposits were found there in 1516. The Counts Schlick minted large silver coins there from 1520, the Joachimsthaler, whose name, shortened to thaler, gave rise to the word dollar. Later its uranium ores yielded the radium isolated by Marie Curie, and under communism prisoners were forced to mine uranium there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jachymov.jpg" alt="Jáchymov" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Devilsanddust · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:J%C3%A1chymov_2016_a.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
